Melomancy in performance. Give bronze, viola, and horn a short phrase of the same length. Introduce them one at a time as the cue travels. Once the cue returns, let them sound together. On a tabletop stage, a raised cross and four textured pegs let a reader follow the quarter-turns by touch. In an audio performance, give the four positions distinct sounds and let the original sound return on the fourth turn.